    {
        "id":  4742,
        "hub_id":  9298,
        "version":  "1.5.2+experimental",
        "description":  "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIF UPDATING FROM A VERSION OLDER THAN 1.4.8, DELETE THE OLD “BorkelRNVG.dll” LOCATED IN “BepInEx/plugins”. LATTEST VERSION HAS A NEW AND MORE ORGANIZED FOLDER STRUCTURE.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor SPT 3.8.0.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImproved the masks for the GPNVG-18 and the T-7.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the GPNVG-18 I’ve horizontally flipped the lense shadows so that they appear on the outer lenses and not the inner ones. This makes more sense, since the outer lenses are the ones that are angled (new is top, old is bottom):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/5ySdAps.png\" alt=\"5ySdAps.png\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe T-7 is viewed through a digital display, not a lense like with NVGs, so I’ve made it look more like a display by cutting its vertical FOV (like the FLIR). The old mask is still available in the optional masks folders. This is how it looks now:\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/zUbYQKo.png\" alt=\"zUbYQKo.png\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
